{%- comment -%}
  The tools an agent may use, for code running inside the app (for example an in-app
  assistant that offers them to a model). A tool is listed when it is registered with a
  valid manifest, the agent's allowed_tools (when set) includes it, and its
  authorization policy admits the principal and agent with empty arguments — the same
  rules tools/list uses with tools_list_scope 'principal', plus the allowed_tools
  narrowing that commands/execute/invoke applies. A policy that needs arguments to
  allow hides the tool here (fail-closed); invoke re-authorizes every call with the real
  arguments regardless.

  Each tool has the MCP wire shape (helpers/registry/present_tool): name, title?,
  description, inputSchema, outputSchema?, annotations?, _meta.

  @param {object} principal         - { id, user_id }
  @param {object} agent             - { id, client_id, token_id?, allowed_tools? }
  @param {string} [delegation_mode] - direct (default) | on_behalf_of
  @return {array} the tools, in registry order
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign tools = []
  if principal.id == blank or agent.client_id == blank
    return tools
  endif
  assign dm = delegation_mode | default: 'direct'
  assign allowed_tools = agent.allowed_tools
  assign narrowed = false
  if allowed_tools != blank and allowed_tools != empty
    assign narrowed = true
  endif
  assign empty_args = {}
  function reg = 'modules/mcp/queries/registry/load'
  for m in reg.tools
    if narrowed
      unless allowed_tools contains m.name
        continue
      endunless
    endif
    function az = 'modules/mcp/commands/authorize/evaluate', policy: m.authorization_policy, principal: principal, agent: agent, arguments: empty_args, tool: m, delegation_mode: dm
    if az.allow == true
      function t = 'modules/mcp/helpers/registry/present_tool', manifest: m
      assign tools = tools | array_add: t
    endif
  endfor
  return tools
%}
